From 8f6c2d3205df3a0aab5c156d3b7e2950eda8beb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicandros Nic <nicandris@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:28:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] greeter: Show authentication messages from PAM
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The daemon forwards PAM's conversation messages to the greeter over the
socket, and GreeterProxy re-emits them as informationMessage(). Nothing
was ever connected to that signal, so the messages were dropped.

This is visible with any PAM module that prompts the user partway through
authentication. With pam_u2f's "cue" option, PAM sends "Please touch the
FIDO authenticator." — the lock screen shows it, but the login screen
showed nothing at all, leaving no indication that authentication was
waiting on a hardware key rather than hung.

Connect the signal to the existing notificationMessage property, which is
already rendered in both the user-list and username-prompt layouts and is
already used to display "Login Failed".

Starting notificationResetTimer from onNotificationMessageChanged cleared
every message after 3 seconds, which is wrong for a prompt the user is
still acting on — the cue would vanish while they were reaching for their
key. onLoginFailed was the only handler that ever set a non-empty message,
so start the timer there instead. Existing behaviour is unchanged, and the
PAM message now stays until handleLoginRequest() clears it on the next
attempt.

CCBUG: 513560
---
 src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml b/src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml
index 56bb4d32..e4891dfb 100644
--- a/src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml
+++ b/src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml
@@ -369,8 +369,16 @@ Item {
     Connections {
         target: PlasmaLogin.Authenticator
 
+        // e.g. pam_u2f's "cue" asking the user to touch their key. Not auto-cleared
+        // like "Login Failed" is: handleLoginRequest() clears it on the next attempt.
+        function onInformationMessage(message) {
+            notificationMessage = message;
+        }
+
         function onLoginFailed() {
             notificationMessage = i18nd("plasma_login", "Login Failed");
+            // Only failures time out; started here rather than on every change.
+            notificationResetTimer.start();
 
             footer.enabled = true;
             mainStack.enabled = true;
@@ -385,12 +393,6 @@ Item {
         }
     }
 
-    onNotificationMessageChanged: {
-        if (notificationMessage) {
-            notificationResetTimer.start();
-        }
-    }
-
     Timer {
         id: notificationResetTimer
         interval: 3000
-- 
